# Withdrawn Rulings (load-bearing)

A retraction does not reach running sessions on its own. When you retract a claim you circulated or published, record it:

```sh
node "$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/hooks/withdrawn-rulings.mjs" --withdraw "<id>" \
  --claim "<claim, verbatim>" --because "<what disproved it>" --derived "<artifact left standing on it>"
```

`--derived` lists what you filed or relayed while you believed the claim. Use `none` if you checked and nothing remains. Correct each item through the channel it went out on. Run `--list` before you escalate where no hook runs.

Detail: [reference/withdrawn-rulings.md](withdrawn-rulings-reference.mdc).
